  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, which passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run it in a browser here, so it hasn't been built with `vite build` or looked at. It builds the forest from three instanced nodes: trunks (8,000 cylinders), canopies (8,000 cones) and rocks (2,000 spheres). Placement uses a fixed-seed generator, so the forest is the same on every load. Canopies and rocks get a different colour per instance, using white base materials so the colours aren't applied twice. The scene also has a ground plane, a hemisphere light, one shadow-casting directional light, and `effects.fog` set to `mode: \"exp\"`. The camera orbits at radius 125 and height 68 by calling `app.camera?.setPose` each frame, and `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame is drawn. Three things are untested guesses. Whether `setPose` actually moves the camera, whether the shadow `fit` extent covers the forest, and whether the camera view frames the whole forest.",
